# Both claim files carry a per-branch note at the same place, so every branch
# that merges main after another branch merged conflicts in both. The notes are
# comments and union; the bare claim lines below them are value-bearing and do
# not. tests/env_drift.py's `claimnotes` driver does exactly that split and
# refuses a claim list both sides rewrote.
#
# Install the driver once per clone (a worktree shares its checkout's config):
#
#     python3 tests/env_drift.py --install-merge-driver
#
# With no driver configured git falls back to its ordinary text merge, so these
# two lines cannot make a fresh clone behave worse than it does today.
tests/golden/claimed_drift.txt merge=claimnotes
tests/golden/card_claimed_drift.txt merge=claimnotes
